  "chunk": "The player seems to realize it should return to the trophy case to drop collected\n9\ntreasures, as instructed as the main goal of the game in the initial advanced\nprompt. Although the player is able to reach the trophy case, it does so with-\nout any collected treasures, as all potential treasures (which items qualify as\ntreasures are not known a priori) were dropped to enable climbing the chim-\nney. Moreover, the player goes back down through the trap door, finding itself\nonce again locked in the basement. From here on it could decide to go back up\nthe chimney with different items (i.e., possible treasures), yet fails to do so in\nsubsequent steps (not shown in Example 3).\nThis discussion and the provided examples suggest that commonsense rea-\nsoning and genuine metacognition appear severely limited in the context of text-\nbased gameplay, with LLM-models showing behaviour that differs substantially\nfrom expected human behaviour. However, the extent to which these domain-",
